From: Gezim <gezimos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Kompakt: turning auto-rotate off locks portrait

LineageOS's configurable rotation angles made setRotationLock keep the
angle the phone is at when that angle is allowed, and 90 and 270 are
allowed by default. Turning auto-rotate off with the phone sideways (in a
car mount) locked it in landscape; every tap of the tile while sideways
locked landscape again, and the saved angle survived a reboot (tester
report, build 460: user_rotation 90 under USER_ROTATION_LOCKED).

The lock now goes to the natural orientation, as in AOSP, unless
config_useCurrentRotationOnRotationLockChange asks for the current one;
getRotationLockOrientation reports that orientation.
---
diff --git a/core/java/com/android/internal/view/RotationPolicy.java b/core/java/com/android/internal/view/RotationPolicy.java
--- a/core/java/com/android/internal/view/RotationPolicy.java
+++ b/core/java/com/android/internal/view/RotationPolicy.java
@@ -78,9 +78,6 @@
      * otherwise Configuration.ORIENTATION_UNDEFINED if any orientation is lockable.
      */
     public static int getRotationLockOrientation(Context context) {
-        if (isCurrentRotationAllowed(context)) {
-            return Configuration.ORIENTATION_UNDEFINED;
-        }
         final DisplayMetrics metrics = context.getResources().getDisplayMetrics();
         final int rotation =
                 context.getResources().getConfiguration().windowConfiguration.getRotation();
@@ -126,8 +123,8 @@
      * Enables or disables rotation lock from the system UI toggle.
      */
     public static void setRotationLock(Context context, final boolean enabled, String caller) {
-        final int rotation = isCurrentRotationAllowed(context)
-                || useCurrentRotationOnRotationLockChange(context) ? CURRENT_ROTATION
+        // Kompakt: locking always returns to the natural orientation, not the angle the phone is at.
+        final int rotation = useCurrentRotationOnRotationLockChange(context) ? CURRENT_ROTATION
                 : getNaturalRotation();
         setRotationLockAtAngle(context, enabled, rotation, caller);
     }
